# TF-904: Rename Parse to ParseInt in the whole package and repair the wrong expectation

## Goal

The package in this Go module has a function named Parse that reads an integer
from a string. The name is too generic, so rename it to ParseInt everywhere in
the package: its definition, every call site in every file, and every test that
calls it. The test TestLoadLimit in config_test.go also expects the wrong value
(7 for the input "5"), so after the rename correct that single expected value
to 5. Only that expected value may change in the tests.

## Dependencies

None

## Scope

Edit the Go files of the package in the module root only. The rename touches
util.go, config.go, cmd.go, and the test files that call it. Do not rename
anything else, and do not change any other test expectation.

## Constraints

Do not add dependencies. Keep the behaviour of every function the same. Commit
the change on the task branch.

## Success criteria

### C1: No old name remains

Check: test -z "$(grep -rnw 'Parse' --include='*.go' .)"

### C2: The package builds and vets

Check: go vet ./...

### C3: The unit tests pass

Check: go test ./...

## Verification

Run each check from the repository root and report its exit code.
